-- title:
--   Node charts, Hasse germ and node centre for q=3
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic frame.** Fixed are a prime $q$ with $q = 3$, a nonzero level $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a guard prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. Further fixed are a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ (i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$), a finite set $W$ of places of the characteristic-$p$ modular function field `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, the inclusion `hle` of the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` of the full modular function field of level $M'$ into `fieldBar q M'` (the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change of the function field of $X_H$ at level $q^2M'$ with $H =$ `levelH q M'`), a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ on `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` with values in `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the source together with a surjective residue map onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal, inducing $A$ and its residue map on constants, with the usual scaling and degree/divisor compatibilities), the hypothesis `hR₀` that for a Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$, and a distinguished supersingular place $s \in W$.
--
--   **Constants, layers, tame data, base presentation.** A subfield $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$ are given such that $A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field (`hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres`), together with `hκ`: every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$. A prime $\ell$ with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$ is given, together with $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity and $\varpi_t \in k_0 \cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q \cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. A layer family consists of a type $\iota$, intermediate fields $K_n$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ each finite over $k_0$, valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K_n$ cut out by $A$, a least index $n_0$ (so $K_{n_0} \le K_n$ for all $n$), and the cofinality hypothesis `hKcof` that every finite subset of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in the image of some $K_n$. A tame parameter $\pi_t \in A$ with $\pi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q$ is given, with `htame`: every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ on which the tame character of $A$ relative to $\pi_t$ is trivial fixes $K_{n_0}$ pointwise. Finally a base presentation: an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ cut out by $A$, and a nonzero generator $\varpi_b$ of its maximal ideal.
--
--   **Level field.** With `fieldBar q M'` viewed as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ satisfying four conditions: $f \in F_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $f$ lies in $k_0$; the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is everything; $F_0$ is stable under each level automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` ($\zeta$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity in the index type `Idx q`, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$); and a linear-disjointness condition: for every finite extension $K'/k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, every family $a_i$ in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, and every $K'$-linearly independent family $c_i$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$.
--
--   **Data quantified over, and the hypothesis block.** For every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$, every subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` with an $A_b$-algebra structure, the integrality datum `hjR` that the image of the $j$-expansion `jq` lies in `R₀.integers`, the datum `hjs` that its $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the datum `hJK` that [`ModularCurve.jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in `fieldBar q M'`, a Hasse lift $a_0 \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue satisfies $\overline{a_0}^{\,q} = s(\,\overline{j}\,)$ (`hpin`: the $q$-th power of the residue of $a_0$ is the value at $s$ of the $R_0$-residue of $j$), and a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$, the following hypothesis block is assumed; its groups are: (i) $W_0$ induces $A$ on $k_0$, is a discrete valuation ring, and has maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$; (ii) a specialisation clause at $s$: for $g$ in the full modular function field of level $M'$ whose barred image is $R_0$-integral and regular at every place where $j$ is, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $g$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue is the value of that $R_0$-residue at $s$ the difference lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$; (iii) invariance of $W_0$ under all `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; (iv) an affine-chart block for $B$: the $A_b$-algebra structure is compatible with $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`, $B$ is contained in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$ and that join is the fraction field of $B$, $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$, $B/\varpi_b B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$, $B$ lies in $W_0$, $\varpi_b$ is prime in $B$, $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\varpi_b$, $j \in B$, $B$ is stable under the level automorphisms, there is an element of $B \cap F_0$ with a pole along every valuation subring of $F_0$ which induces $A$ on $k_0$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, contains $j$ and makes $p(j)$ a unit for every monic $p$ with $A$-integral $k_0$-coefficients, and likewise, for each $s' \in W$ with $s' \ne s$, an element of $B \cap F_0$ with a pole along every valuation subring of $F_0$ satisfying the specialisation clause at $s'$; (v) a Drinfeld-reduction clause: for every $(\mathbb{F}_{q^2})$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$ making [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) a domain, and every $\zeta$, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity in $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ of order $2\,\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` and a ring map $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q (ResidueField A) Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) with kernel $\varpi_b B$, compatible with reduction on $A_b$, whose image generates the target as a field of fractions and consists exactly of the elements coming from [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21), and which intertwines `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` with [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) for those $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{red}_q\gamma, 1)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276); (vi) a node block: `nodes` has $q+1$ elements; there is a subring $B_c$ of $F_0$ generated over $k_0 \cap A$ by a finite set which is contained in every node and of which every node is the localisation at its own units; the level automorphisms permute `nodes` and act transitively on it; distinct nodes are separated by an element which is a non-unit in one and a unit in the other; every valuation subring of $F_0$ inducing $A$ on $k_0$ and satisfying the specialisation clause at $s$ either contains $B$ or dominates some node; and for each node $\mathcal{O}$: $\mathcal{O} \subseteq W_0$, $\mathcal{O}$ is local and Noetherian, induces $A$ on $k_0$, every element of $\mathcal{O}$ differs from a constant in $k_0 \cap A$ by a non-unit, and there exist an exponent $E_0 \ge 1$ with $\pi_0^{E_0} = \varpi_t^{\,2\,\mathrm{pwc}} v$ for a unit $v$ of $k_0 \cap A$ (where $\mathrm{pwc} =$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`), elements $c_x, c_y \in \mathcal{O}$, a unit $u$ of $\mathcal{O}$, a ring isomorphism of the adic completion of $\mathcal{O}$ with the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` over the adic completion of $A \cap k_0$ with parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$, and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that crossing model, such that $c_x c_y = \pi_0^{E_0} u$, the isomorphism carries constants to `const`, carries $c_x$ to $\gamma_U \cdot U$ and $c_y$ to $\gamma_V \cdot V$, $c_y$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$ while $c_x$ is a unit there, the Hasse germ $J - a_0$ (with $J =$ `jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q`) lies in $F_0$ and in $\mathcal{O}$ and is carried to a unit times $V^e$ with $e \ge 1$, there is an Igusa branch: a discrete valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ containing $\mathcal{O}$, inducing $A$ on $k_0$, with uniformiser $\pi_0$, carrying an element whose residue is transcendental over the residue field (no monic relation with $A$-integral coefficients becomes singular unless all coefficients do), in which $c_x$ is a non-unit and $c_y$ a unit, along which the $R_0$-integral modular functions regular where $j$ is specialise with vanishing detected by vanishing of the $R_0$-residue and with the node-specialisation behaviour at $s$, and such that every other node contains a function not in $W_x$; and finally a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ inside $B \cap \mathcal{O}$, consisting of functions regular wherever $j$ is, of which $\mathcal{O}$ is the localisation at its units, whose fraction field is $F_0$, which is generated over $k_0 \cap A$ by a finite set, and which contains an element with a pole along every valuation subring that induces $A$ on $k_0$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, contains $j$ with $j$ avoiding every monic $A$-integral relation, and fails to dominate $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under that block, for every field $F_{SS}$ which is an algebra over the residue field of $A$ and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ on `fieldBar q M'` with values in $F_{SS}$ such that $R$-integrality on $F_0$ coincides with membership in $W_0$, there is a finite set $N$ of places of $F_{SS}$ over the residue field of $A$ with $|N| = q+1$, and there exist: fields $F_{Ix}$ indexed by the places of $F_{SS}$, each an algebra over the residue field of $A$, regular prolongations $R_x$ of $A$ on `fieldBar q M'` with values in them, places $b_x$ of those fields; subrings $C'_l \subseteq A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ which are discrete valuation domains with uniformisers $\varpi'_l$; complete discrete valuation rings $W_{c,l}$ with uniformisers $\pi_l$, exponents $E_l$ and an exponent $E_0$; sets $S(nd)$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, subrings $\mathcal{N}(nd)$ and local Noetherian subrings $\mathcal{N}_0(nd, l)$ of `fieldBar q M'`, and elements $c_x(nd), c_y(nd), c_u(nd)$ of `fieldBar q M'`, subject to the following.
--
--   First, $C'_n$ consists exactly of the elements of $A$ lying in $K_n$; the residue of $d \in C'_l$ in $A$ vanishes if and only if $\varpi'_l \mid d$; $C'_{n_0} \le C'_l$ for all $l$; $\varpi'_{n_0} \ne 0$; every element of $A$ is algebraic over $C'_{n_0}$; each $\pi_l$ is irreducible and $E_l \ge 1$; every inertia element of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ with trivial tame character relative to $\pi_t$ fixes $\varpi'_{n_0}$; and there are $w \ge 1$ and a unit $v$ of $A$ with $(\varpi'_{n_0})^{E_0} = v\,\pi_t^{\,w}$.
--
--   Second, for each $nd \in N$: there is a node $\mathcal{O} \in$ `nodes` whose image lies in $\mathcal{N}_0(nd, n_0)$ with non-units going to non-units, such that $S(nd)$ is exactly the set of places $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` dominating $\mathcal{O}$ (all of $\mathcal{O}$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$, and the value at $P$ of each non-unit of $\mathcal{O}$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$), such that the $R$-residues of elements of $\mathcal{O}$ lie in the valuation subring of $nd$ with non-units landing in its maximal ideal, and such that $nd$ is the unique place of $F_{SS}$ with these two properties. The places $b_x(nd)$, $nd$ and all $P \in S(nd)$ are rational (the constants surject onto their residue fields). The ring $\mathcal{N}(nd)$ consists of those $f$ which are $R_x(nd)$-integral, $R$-integral, and lie in every valuation subring of $S(nd)$; for such $f$ and $P \in S(nd)$ the value $P(f)$ lies in $A$. The crossing relation $c_x(nd)\,c_y(nd) = (\varpi'_{n_0})^{E_0} c_u(nd)$ holds; $c_x(nd)$ has vanishing $R_x(nd)$-residue and its $R$-residue has $nd$-order $1$; $c_y(nd)$ has vanishing $R$-residue and its $R_x(nd)$-residue has $b_x(nd)$-order $1$. For every inertia element $\tau$ with trivial tame character, the induced semilinear automorphism [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')) τ`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) preserves $S(nd)$ and fixes $c_x(nd)$ and $c_y(nd)$. Every $f \in$ `fieldBar q M'` is a ratio of two elements of some $\mathcal{N}_0(nd, l)$, and also becomes, after multiplication by a nonzero element of $\mathcal{N}_0(nd, n_0)$, a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-linear combination of elements of $\mathcal{N}_0(nd, n_0)$.
--
--   Third, for each layer $l$: $\mathcal{N}_0(nd, n_0) \le \mathcal{N}_0(nd, l) \le \mathcal{N}(nd)$; $S(nd)$ is equally characterised by domination of $\mathcal{N}_0(nd, l)$; the constants $C'_l$ map into $\mathcal{N}_0(nd, l)$; every element of $\mathcal{N}_0(nd, l)$ differs from such a constant by a non-unit; families of elements of $\mathcal{N}_0(nd, l)$ with $C'_l$-linearly independent $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-coefficients summing to zero vanish; there is a subring $B_x \subseteq \mathcal{N}_0(nd, l)$ containing $c_x(nd), c_y(nd), c_u(nd)$, of which $\mathcal{N}_0(nd, l)$ is the localisation at its units, generated by the $C'_l$-constants together with a finite set; $c_x(nd), c_y(nd) \in \mathcal{N}_0(nd, l)$ and $c_u(nd)$ is a unit there; and there are a ring map $\sigma$ from $W_{c,l}$ to the adic completion of $\mathcal{N}_0(nd, l)$ and a ring isomorphism $\iota_c$ of that completion with `UVCrossingModel (Wc l) (π l ^ E l)` such that $\sigma(\pi_l)$ is the image of $\varpi'_l$, $\iota_c \circ \sigma$ is the constant embedding, the Hasse germ $J - a_0$ lies in $\mathcal{N}_0(nd, l)$ and is carried by $\iota_c$ to a unit times $V^e$ with $e \ge 1$, every $C'_l$-constant is in the image of $\sigma$, and the two order dictionaries hold: an element whose $R_x(nd)$-residue is nonzero of $b_x(nd)$-order $n$ is congruent under $\iota_c$ to a unit times $V^n$ modulo the ideal generated by `const (π l)` and $U$, and an element whose $R$-residue is nonzero of $nd$-order $n$ is congruent to a unit times $U^n$ modulo the ideal generated by `const (π l)` and $V$.
--
--   Fourth, the sets $S(nd)$ for $nd \in N$ are pairwise disjoint. Fifth, for $nd \in N$ and $P \in S(nd)$, every $R_0$-integral $f$ regular where $j$ is and with $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$ satisfies: for every $a \in A$ whose residue is the value at $s$ of that $R_0$-residue, $P(f) - a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$. Sixth, for each $\zeta'$ and each $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ there is a self-map $\tau_N$ of the places of $F_{SS}$ preserving $N$, transporting the discs ($(\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,\zeta'\,\gamma) \cdot P \in S(nd)$ if and only if $P \in S(\tau_N nd)$) and matching the prolongations ($R_x(nd)$-integrality pulled back along the automorphism is $R_x(\tau_N nd)$-integrality). Seventh, for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the level automorphisms with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $R$-integrality, and every $nd \in N$, the residual automorphism `R.resAut` moves $nd$ inside $N$ and carries $S(nd)$ to $S$ of the image, in the sense of [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.smulDisc`](def/AlgebraicCurve_ResidueDiscs.html#L120). Eighth, $R_0$-integral elements are $R_x(nd)$-integral for all $nd \in N$. Ninth, for each $nd \in N$ there is a ring map $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` to $F_{Ix}(nd)$ which computes $R_x(nd)$-residues of $R_0$-integral elements from their $R_0$-residues and which pulls back the valuation subring of $b_x(nd)$ to that of $s$. Tenth, distinct $nd, nd' \in N$ are separated: there is $g$ lying in $\mathcal{N}_0(nd, n_0)$ and in $\mathcal{N}_0(nd', n_0)$ which is $c_x(nd)$ times a unit in the former and a unit in the latter.
--
--   This is the per-node core of the layered presentation of the nodes of the semistable model at the prime $q = 3$ (at a rigid auxiliary level forced by the guard prime $\ell_g \equiv 11 \bmod 12$): starting from a level field $F_0$ with its affine chart $B$ and its finite set of node rings, it produces the $q+1$ node places of the supersingular fibre above $s$, their node discs, their layered local rings with $uv$-crossing completions, the Igusa germ of the Hasse invariant, and the transport of all this by the level automorphisms and by inertia. It is cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_of_eq_three_of_dvd), which assembles the node presentations of the special fibre.
